## Experimental Results (selected)

- Complex physics problem-solving: **82 / 93** (manually assisted structured inputs)
- Compositional reasoning: **300 / 300** (controlled multi-step knowledge-composition tasks)
- Knowledge-driven planning: **17 vs. 6** optimal plans out of 24 tasks (with vs. without validated knowledge reuse)
- Scientific law learning: **40 / 40** validated relationships
- Trajectory prediction: **6,000 / 6,000** evaluated checkpoints across 200 trajectories (using supplied motion laws)

Notes: these results were obtained under structured evaluation settings; they demonstrate the feasibility of the architecture under controlled conditions while clarifying current limits.

---

## Current Research Extensions

- LLM–KNWM integration: an AGI-oriented system where the LLM handles language I/O and KNWM handles knowledge, reasoning, and planning; includes an initial capability-expansion mechanism to generate and retain new capabilities.
- 3D perception: connecting structured visual observations (3D) to knowledge neurons for richer state descriptions.
- Embodied planning: adapting knowledge-driven planning to embodied agents under changing environmental constraints.

These directions are ongoing research work, not claims of fully deployed real-world systems.

